# Claiming units

Import CoordinatorDb from "./coordinator_db.lg".

A worker's lease, taken from the database in one statement. Without a focus the
schema's own `factory.claim_unit` takes it: expired leases return to the board,
and the best-priority ready unit of the asked kinds is leased under a fresh,
larger fencing token, skipping any unit another claim holds. With a focus the
same claim is made over the units whose problem is the focus or lies in it (its
cohort, collection or category).

When nothing fits, the coordinator plans: it queues units for the best-ranked
open problems that have none, and claims again. The board therefore never runs
dry while open problems remain, and is never planned further ahead than workers
ask.

## Note
A PostgreSQL array literal of kinds. The kinds have been checked against the
leasable vocabulary, so none holds a comma, a brace or a quote.

## To kindsArray (kinds: Seq of Text) -> Text:
    Return "{{" + join(kinds, ",") + "}}".

## Note
The claimed unit as JSON (`unitId`, `token`), or an empty object for none.

## To claimSql () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["SELECT coalesce((SELECT json_build_object('unitId', c.unit_id, 'token', c.token)"].
    Push "FROM factory.claim_unit($1, $2::int, $3::text[]) AS c), '{{}}'::json)::text" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## To focusedClaimSql () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["WITH expired AS (UPDATE factory.work_unit w SET state = 'ready', holder = NULL, lease_token = NULL, leased_at = NULL,"].
    Push "expires_at = NULL, heartbeat_at = NULL WHERE w.state = 'leased' AND w.expires_at < clock_timestamp() RETURNING w.id)," to q.
    Push "pick AS (SELECT u.id FROM factory.work_unit u JOIN factory.problem p ON p.id = u.problem_id WHERE u.state = 'ready'" to q.
    Push "AND u.kind = ANY ($3::text[]) AND $4 IN (p.id, p.cohort, p.collection, p.category)" to q.
    Push "ORDER BY u.priority DESC, u.created_at LIMIT 1 FOR UPDATE OF u SKIP LOCKED)," to q.
    Push "taken AS (UPDATE factory.work_unit w SET state = 'leased', holder = $1, lease_token = nextval('factory.lease_token')," to q.
    Push "leased_at = clock_timestamp(), heartbeat_at = clock_timestamp(), expires_at = clock_timestamp() + make_interval(secs => $2::int / 1000.0)" to q.
    Push "FROM pick WHERE w.id = pick.id RETURNING w.id, w.lease_token)" to q.
    Push "SELECT coalesce((SELECT json_build_object('unitId', id, 'token', lease_token) FROM taken), '{{}}'::json)::text" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## Note
Units for the best-ranked open problems without one: `prove` for a problem with
an accepted statement, `formalize` for one with no statement under review. `$1`
is how many, `$2` the kinds asked, `$3` the focus or the empty text.

## To planSql () -> Text:
    Let mutable q be ["INSERT INTO factory.work_unit (id, problem_id, statement_id, kind, priority, state)"].
    Push "SELECT 'u:' || gen_random_uuid()::text, x.id, x.sid, x.kind, x.rank, 'ready' FROM (SELECT p.id, s.id AS sid, p.rank," to q.
    Push "CASE WHEN s.id IS NULL THEN 'formalize' ELSE 'prove' END AS kind FROM factory.problem p" to q.
    Push "LEFT JOIN factory.statement s ON s.problem_id = p.id AND s.review_state = 'accepted'" to q.
    Push "LEFT JOIN factory.node n ON n.problem_id = p.id AND n.kind = 'problem' WHERE p.status = 'open'" to q.
    Push "AND coalesce(n.stage, 'ranked') NOT IN ('solved', 'refuted', 'partial', 'invalid_formalization')" to q.
    Push "AND ($3 = '' OR $3 IN (p.id, p.cohort, p.collection, p.category))" to q.
    Push "AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM factory.work_unit u WHERE u.problem_id = p.id AND u.state IN ('ready', 'leased'))" to q.
    Push "AND (s.id IS NOT NULL OR NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM factory.statement d WHERE d.problem_id = p.id" to q.
    Push "AND d.review_state IN ('draft', 'reviewing')))) AS x WHERE x.kind = ANY ($2::text[]) ORDER BY x.rank DESC, x.id LIMIT $1::int" to q.
    Return join(q, " ").

## Note
One claim on an open connection: the unit and token as JSON, or an empty object.

## To claimOn (c: PgConn, holder: Text, ttlMs: Int, kinds: Seq of Text, focus: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    If focus is equal to "":
        Return dbCellOn(c, claimSql(), [holder, "{ttlMs}", kindsArray(kinds)]).
    Return dbCellOn(c, focusedClaimSql(), [holder, "{ttlMs}", kindsArray(kinds), focus]).

## Note
A claim, planning once and claiming again when the board had nothing that fits.

## To claimOrPlan (c: PgConn, holder: Text, ttlMs: Int, kinds: Seq of Text, focus: Text) -> Result of Text and Text:
    Inspect claimOn(c, holder, ttlMs, kinds, focus):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (first):
            If first is not equal to "{{}}":
                Return a new Ok with value first.
    Inspect pgQueryParams(c, planSql(), ["8", kindsArray(kinds), focus]):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error e.
        When Ok (planned):
            Return claimOn(c, holder, ttlMs, kinds, focus).
    Return a new Err with error "no claim".
